WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:03.669
Dear Fellow Scholars, we have some delightful news!

00:00:03.669 --> 00:00:09.020
Elon Musk and Sam Altman founded a non-profit
artificial intelligence research company that

00:00:09.020 --> 00:00:15.970
they call OpenAI. The funders have committed
over one billion dollars for this cause. Their

00:00:15.970 --> 00:00:20.810
goal is to make progress towards superintelligence,
leveraging their non-profit nature to make

00:00:20.810 --> 00:00:25.039
sure that such a breakthrough will be done
in a controlled and beneficial way.

00:00:25.039 --> 00:00:29.390
As of the current state of things, most of
the bigger companies with strong AI groups

00:00:29.390 --> 00:00:34.039
publish their work regularly, but as we get
closer to Artificial General Intelligence

00:00:34.039 --> 00:00:38.239
and superintelligence, it is a question how
much they will share.

00:00:38.239 --> 00:00:42.979
We have talked already about how enormously
powerful a superintelligence could become,

00:00:42.979 --> 00:00:47.530
and how important it is to make sure that
it is developed in a safe way, make sure to

00:00:47.530 --> 00:00:52.149
check that video out, a link is in the description
box. It is really mind blowing.

00:00:52.149 --> 00:00:57.149
So everything they create will be open, therefore
the first question that came to my mind - is

00:00:57.149 --> 00:01:02.399
really good that anyone will be able to create
an AI? What about users who are interested

00:01:02.399 --> 00:01:08.430
in using it in a way that is harmful and dangerous
to others? This was subject to a lot of debate,

00:01:08.430 --> 00:01:13.570
and one of the conclusions is that at the
same time, most people are sensible, and they

00:01:13.570 --> 00:01:18.600
expect that the number of friendly AIs will
overpower the bad guys. We don't know if it's

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:23.630
the best case scenario, but it is definitely
better than the case of one company owning

00:01:23.630 --> 00:01:25.840
the only superintelligence.

00:01:25.840 --> 00:01:30.100
At OpenAI, they already have researchers of
their own, and their research projects will

00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:36.060
be completely open. This is amazing, because
it rarely happens with companies as they usually

00:01:36.060 --> 00:01:39.490
want to retain the intellectual property of
their projects.

00:01:39.490 --> 00:01:44.590
Amazon web services are also donating a huge
amount of resources for the company.

00:01:44.590 --> 00:01:50.010
The fact that just like at research institutions,
the researchers can publicly share their work

00:01:50.010 --> 00:01:54.920
may be a big deciding factor when recruiting,
which is, according to the founders, already

00:01:54.920 --> 00:01:55.970
going really well.

00:01:58.810 --> 00:02:02.369
Thanks for watching and for your generous
support, and I'll see you next time!

